      verdict:
        "Both live in the e-commerce lane; the split is market radius: one says buy in German, the other says shop to the world. .kaufen wins on search-intent match — German-market e-commerce shops, price-comparison and deals platforms, second-hand marketplaces and DACH promo landing pages on name.kaufen say \"buy here\" in one word; kaufen is German for to buy, the exact word German speakers put in their searches (auto kaufen), so category + .kaufen reads like a call to action that matches the query letter for letter; the registry is Identity Digital, open since 2014; about {{price:kaufen:first:usd}} first year ({{price:kaufen:first:cny}}) and {{price:kaufen:renew:usd}}/yr to renew ({{price:kaufen:renew:cny}}) — the cheap first year suits experiments, budget on the renewal, which sits in the gentle tier among commerce suffixes. .shop wins on global recognition — independent stores and DTC brand shops, vertical-category commerce, and offline stores' online entrances on name.shop make brand + .shop a call to action in itself, with the largest registration base and most mature user recognition among e-commerce suffixes, plus deep inventory; first-year promos are common while renewals run notably higher — budget on the renewal. The test: the audience is the German-speaking region — commerce and promo business in Germany, Austria and Switzerland where German search traffic is the main channel → .kaufen matches search intent word for word, a localization signal a generic suffix can't send; the audience is global — cross-border commerce, multilingual stores, DTC brands for international markets → .shop's worldwide recognition is steadier, readable in any language. A common combo: the global store fronts on .shop while the DACH promo entrance stands on category or brand + .kaufen to catch German search traffic. Three cautions: .kaufen's audience is the German-speaking region — users outside it won't read it, so don't make it a global store's primary domain; German e-commerce is bound by price-display and withdrawal-right consumer law, so promo pages must comply; and both are cheap in year one with different renewal structures, so price a multi-domain portfolio on three years of renewals. Naming: category + .kaufen (auto.kaufen) maps one-to-one to the German search phrase; brand + .shop (acme.shop) is the standard global storefront.",
